Subcommand Description <code>sensor list</code> Show every sensor, its bit and ON/off state <code>sensor enable &lt;name\|all&gt;</code> Turn a sensor on (RAM, then <code>config save</code>) <code>sensor disable &lt;name\|all&gt;</code> Turn a sensor off (RAM, then <code>config save</code>) <code>sensor read</code> Init, read and deinit every enabled sensor, printing JSON <code>sensor read &lt;name&gt;</code> Read one sensor, even if it is disabled <code>sensor read all</code> Read every registered sensor <p>Registered sensors: <code>BME280</code>, <code>SHT3x</code>, <code>BH1750</code>, <code>MH-Z19</code>, <code>PMS5003</code>, <code>Moisture</code>, <code>DS18B20</code>.</p> <pre><code>&gt; sensor read BME280
[BME280] {"temperature":22.4,"humidity":41.2,"pressure":1008.3}
</code></pre> <p>An error such as <code>init FAILED: ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND</code> usually means wiring or a wrong I²C address. Use <code>i2c scan</code> to check.</p>
